**Why C**
- 30% context won't cover tasks 8–9. Auto-compaction (A, D) fires at an arbitrary point, likely mid-commit; B interrupts now. A directed compact at a task boundary is controlled loss, verified afterwards.
- noVNC on `feat/rdp-audio` mixes two changes in one PR and breaks worktree-per-task. A fresh tab starts now, in parallel.

```
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree add .claude/worktrees/novnc-kbd -b fix/novnc-kbd main
herdr tab create --workspace <id> --cwd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/novnc-kbd --label novnc-kbd --no-focus
# brief: systematic-debugging → TDD → verification-before-completion → code review; roles/desktop only

# background, every 30s until the task-7 commit shows
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 40

# at the boundary
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items" --wait --until idle --timeout 360000
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "One line: DIR, branch, HEAD SHA, current task, open items" --wait --until idle
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio rev-parse --short HEAD
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Continue with task 8"
```

Then I update `orchestrator/backlog.md` and the artifact.

**To the operator:** "rdp-audio stays untouched until task 7 is committed, then gets one ~4-minute directed compact; otherwise it auto-compacts mid-task. I put noVNC in its own tab `novnc-kbd` instead of rdp-audio as you asked: it starts now, and the PRs stay separate. Tell me if you want it moved."

CHOICE: C
